  {"id": "L1r", "name": "Shade reflector share of L1 (white enamel interior, 4.4 eta 0.60)", "group": "table_lamp_reflector", "type": "rect", "pos": [13.29916, 5.43496, 1.752], "rot": [-90, 1.5, 0], "size_m": [0.10, 0.10], "barn_door": [50.2, 0.15], "flux_lm": 260, "cct_k": 2700, "specular": 0.0, "shadows": [true, true, true], "vol": 1.0, "vol_shadow": true, "states": {"Open": 1.0, "LightsUp": 1.0, "AfterHours": 1.0},
   "note": "4.4: the modelled lamp is I(theta) = I0 cos(theta), I0 = 355.9 cd, cut-off 50.2 deg; the bare bulb gives 87.5 cd isotropic and Lumen bounces part of the rest off the white enamel interior; this hidden share (Specular 0: the ball highlight stays the bulb's) carries the shortfall Lumen leaves, as 4.4 prescribes ('flux = the measured shortfall'). Measured with the rendered white card (capture_divebar.py --lux, lamp only, Lumen GI on; greybox shades): bulbs + Lumen alone gave centre 391 / rail side 244 / rail corner ~73 lux, the 800 lm share of v1 (sized for direct light only) doubled the bands (centre ~1450, rail side 1046) -> 260 lm. Re-measure when M2-B's lamp body replaces the greybox shades. The shade shadows both beyond the cut-off; the barn doors keep the cut-off without a shade mesh."},
